\ Test stack-shuffling words from prelude

\ nip ( a b -- b ) - removes second item
1 2 nip

\ keep ( x quot -- ... x ) - execute quot, preserve x
drop 5 [ dup + ] keep

\ bi ( x p q -- ) - apply two quotations to one value
2drop 5 [ dup + ] [ 1 + ] bi

\ 2dup ( a b -- a b a b ) - duplicate top two items
2drop 1 2 2dup

\ 2drop ( a b -- ) - drop top two items
2drop 2drop 1 2 3 4 2drop

\ <rot- ( a b c -- b c a ) - bring third item to top
2drop 1 2 3 <rot-

\ -rot> ( a b c -- c a b ) - send top item to third position
drop drop drop 1 2 3 -rot>

\ tuck ( a b -- b a b ) - copy top item below second
drop drop drop 1 2 tuck

\ choose ( a1 a2 quot -- a ) - apply quot to copies, select based on result
drop drop drop 3 5 [ < ] choose

\ choose with false result
drop 5 3 [ < ] choose
